<section class="ls-section dark"><div class="ls-wrap"><div class="ls-head"><span class="ls-kicker" style="color:#b8df85">WHAT WE BUILD</span><h2>One connected system. Not five disconnected tools.</h2><p>The goal is to make campaigns, lead capture, qualification and booked appointments work together—with visibility into where each lead came from.</p></div><div class="ls-grid3"><article class="ls-card ls-capability" data-ls-capability="0" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-pressed="true" aria-controls="ls-capability-panel"><span>01 / ATTRACT</span><h3>Google Search &amp; local visibility</h3><p>Match keywords and service areas to actual offerings, from hardscape installation to maintenance routes. Separate high-intent categories where the buyer need differs.</p></article><article class="ls-card ls-capability" data-ls-capability="1" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="ls-capability-panel"><span>02 / CREATE</span><h3>Meta Ads &amp; visual creative</h3><p>Use project imagery, seasonal offers and relevant local messaging to reach homeowners and property decision-makers without promising arbitrary lead counts.</p></article><article class="ls-card ls-capability" data-ls-capability="2" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="ls-capability-panel"><span>03 / CONVERT</span><h3>Landing pages &amp; qualification</h3><p>Build mobile-first offers, clear forms, calls and project-specific questions. A patio inquiry should not be handled like a weekly mowing request.</p></article><article class="ls-card ls-capability" data-ls-capability="3" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="ls-capability-panel"><span>04 / FOLLOW UP</span><h3>CRM &amp; automation</h3><p>Route leads by service and location, notify the right team and keep follow-up visible. Integrate suitable existing tools rather than replacing working systems without reason.</p></article><article class="ls-card ls-capability" data-ls-capability="4" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="ls-capability-panel"><span>05 / BOOK</span><h3>Appointment setting</h3><p>Organize callbacks, site visits, estimates and design consultations with the context the sales or estimating team needs.</p></article><article class="ls-card ls-capability" data-ls-capability="5" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="ls-capability-panel"><span>06 / IMPROVE</span><h3>Measurement beyond CPL</h3><p>Compare inquiry volume with qualified leads, booked estimates, show rates and the jobs actually won, where the business tracks those outcomes.</p></article></div></div>
