    <section class="ls-section alt"><div class="ls-wrap"><div class="ls-head"><span class="ls-kicker">A PRACTICAL ROADMAP</span><h2>Build demand. Then make it count.</h2><p>Better lead generation starts with the economics of your service mix and follows the inquiry all the way to the estimate.</p></div><div class="ls-grid3"><div class="ls-step"><strong>01 — Define the right work</strong><p>Prioritize profitable services, service areas, route density, job size and schedule capacity before setting up campaigns.</p></div><div class="ls-step"><strong>02 — Match intent and creative</strong><p>Separate lawn care, landscape installation and commercial searches. Build ads and pages that reflect the actual service requested.</p></div><div class="ls-step"><strong>03 — Qualify and route</strong><p>Ask only what is needed to confirm fit, then connect the inquiry to a responsible person, CRM stage or booking step.</p></div></div></div></section>
